"[Experiment] marks souls from another world reborn as monsters under a god's watch."
"[Experiment] protects its holder in a dungeon until the holder attacks."
"Experiments cannot explain [Experiment] to monsters; the words will not come."
"[Unique] marks a being unlike any other of its kind, and wards off prying spirits."
"Earth reincarnators may carry an Otherworlder-type Emblem; asking about it is censored."
"A dungeon master under a god is protected by a rule of no interference until attacked."
"Some dungeon masters are promoted to godhood; Unc once ran a jellyfish dungeon."
"A slime's [Dungeon Master] usurpation hangs \"pending\" while gods argue who oversees it."
"The Mother of Magic urged a favourite to usurp a [Dungeon Master] Emblem."
"A dead elf's legacy Emblem was at risk when she ordered her bonded slime to kill her."
